  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-15T01:31:38.625Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'd like to suggest a lot of graphics options be added to the settings menu. It makes no sense that you have to know a special shortcut for graphic options. On top of that, there's so much room for optimization to be had here.\n\nNot only would it be helpful for the game to have a setup option when launching via steam, an even better option would be to have a separate button/tab in Settings for graphics control.\n\n It could include things like sliders to toggle how many particles you see at a time, a disable dynamic bones option (if possible), and possibly other level of detail options. This could not only help desktop users enjoy the experience, but also VR users who don't want their eyes burnt by particle effects or too many dynamic bones on screen. It's a better solution than just blocking avatars. I don't want to have to talk to a bunch of grey men just because a particle lagged me.\n\nAnother possibility could be that you could disable particles on a certain user, but not their actual avatar.\n\nI'm aware that there seems to be a way to control particles now, but it's a configuration file. Not everyone knows that exists, and I feel like having a separate and more visible menu for a lot of these options would be super helpful and more new-user friendly.\n\nThanks for considering!",
